{"duration_api_ms":22293,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8bbc8b67-6d57-4b93-ad4d-4545904fcd22","total_cost_usd":0.1587126,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15902,"cache_read_input_tokens":165573,"output_tokens":2302,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":841},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15902},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":2302,"cacheReadInputTokens":165573,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15902,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1587126,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":841,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've changed `Hijack` so it now works after the headers have been written but before any body bytes. It still returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten` once body data has been written. The full test suite passes.\n\n- **What was wrong:** the earlier hijack fix (#4295) checked `Written()`, which is already true once headers are flushed by `WriteHeaderNow` but no body bytes have been written yet. Websocket libraries can hit that state just before they hijack, so they got an error.\n- **The fix** (`response_writer.go:111`): the check is now `w.size > 0`, with a short comment explaining why. Hijacking with nothing written still works as before.\n- **Test** (`response_writer_test.go`): I added a case, \"hijack after header write should succeed\", to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`. It failed before the fix with `gin: response already written` and passes after it.\n- **Checks:** `go test -count=1 ./...` passed in every package, and `go vet .` and `gofmt -l .` reported nothing.\n\nThe repo is in detached HEAD and nothing is committed yet. If you want, I'll commit it on a branch using your line as the message.","ttft_ms":4746,"type":"result","duration_ms":29935,"uuid":"44cfd563-bf62-4923-9573-f72e7d58575b","ttft_stream_ms":890,"time_to_request_ms":98,"first_content_frame_ms":891,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
